   "created_at": "2026-11-08T19:38:13Z",
   "updated_at": "2026-11-08T19:38:13Z",
   "body": "Fixed on a fresh fork branch based on main b1e8eb15: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/4878-rune-clip-current (commit 5ba743116cb6f43a10de6024580f5fa96ab8c8c8).\n\nclip keeps its existing 300-byte budget and all callers; when the boundary falls inside a UTF-8 rune, it backs up to that rune's start before adding the ellipsis. This is smaller than my older unpublished branch, which also generalized unrelated clipping sites.\n\nTestOneOffErrRuneBoundary exercises the actual oneOffErr error string with the three-byte ❯ at offsets 297, 298, 299 and 300. On clean main it fails with invalid UTF-8 at offset 298; with the patch it checks the exact whole-rune result. Focused warmup/usage tests under -race, go vet -tags nogui ./internal/gateway, go build -tags nogui ./internal/gateway, gofmt and git diff --check passed.\n\nA broader Claude test selection also ran and failed TestClaudeClientCacheAbsentUnchanged; I have not claimed that selection or the full suite green. No real Claude account or rendered error card was exercised.\n",
